6. WHAT I COULD NOT DO
================================================================================

No QEMU locally, so both plants ran in CI and all kernel observation is from the
uploaded serial artifacts. Did not test a file larger than the 512-byte read
chunk (the corpus file used is small; the multi-chunk path is the K5a F6 finding
again, still unexercised here). Did not attempt to prove mmap/munmap across
process exit; the F4 cleanup finding from the F2.8 review (dead user-stack free
branch) is unchanged by these commits.

================================================================================
7. VERDICT
================================================================================

Both commits do what they claim. The fs:read gate is enforced with a logged
denial (plant H turns exactly that check red), the guard page is unmapped and
faults with P=0/U=1 (plant I turns exactly that check red), and the isolation
check reads A's physical frame through the kernel's own page-table walk rather
than trusting either process. The two test-level defects are N2 (measurement
order) and N4 (PROT_NONE not honoured); neither makes a passing claim false that
is not already qualified in the code.

VERDICT: PASS (N1 to N5 recorded; N2 and N4 should be fixed in the next K6
commit, not reopened here)
